## Approved Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, PixiJS |
| Backend | NestJS, TypeScript, REST |
| Database | PostgreSQL 16+ with pgvector |
| ORM | Prisma (raw SQL only where Prisma cannot express the operation) |
| ML | Python 3.11+, Sentence Transformers, scikit-learn, HDBSCAN, UMAP-learn |
| Local LLM | Ollama (optional, never mandatory for core features) |
| Testing | Jest, Playwright (TS), Pytest (Python) |
| Infrastructure | Docker Compose (local dev) |

**Do not introduce Redis, Kafka, Kubernetes, Spark, Celery, or other unapproved infrastructure without documented justification.**

---

## Component Boundaries — Strictly Enforced

- **Frontend** (`apps/web/`): UI only. Consumes the NestJS API. No direct database access. No ML.
- **Backend** (`apps/api/`): Business logic, REST API, TMDB integration, Prisma. No ML computation.
- **Python ML** (`ml/`): Embedding generation, clustering, UMAP, scoring. Runs as offline/on-demand scripts. Not a persistent service.
- **Database**: Single PostgreSQL instance with pgvector. No second data store.

Data flows from ML → PostgreSQL → NestJS API → Next.js frontend. It never flows the other way.

